      passage: "A delta stands only because the river keeps replacing what the sea takes away: waves and currents strip sediment from the delta's front while fresh mud arrives from upstream. A large reservoir interrupts that supply. Water slows as it spreads into the still pool behind a dam, and most of the sediment it was carrying settles to the reservoir floor rather than continuing downstream. It follows that where a river has been dammed far upstream, ______",
