      passage: "Conservators often find a painting under a varnish applied generations after the picture was made. Such coatings turn yellow and slightly cloudy with age, and a yellow film passes warm light more readily than cool light. When a small window of old varnish is cleared from a landscape, the greens and blues underneath almost always look colder and clearer than the same passages seen through the coating that remains. From this it can be inferred that ______",
